From 01660d25ba890861acbda26e450f9238f5db87fa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 16:47:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 03/11] cross-stream: TALK: the Talk screen keeps its picture
 (GBA): scenes below are not redrawn, panel / strip redrawn only on change,
 the line box on a kept band; sliced generation on the GBA; S3-TALK

talk_scene.c is the TALK stream's. Talk is an overlay scene, so the scene below it (24 ms for the
title) was drawn every tick. scene_keep_below (scene.c, SPEED's) lets Talk ask to be the only
scene drawn: plat_hold_frame keeps the page, hk_* redraws the panel and the people strip on
top of themselves (ui_shadow_kept: no second drop shadow) and the dialogue box draws on a kept
band (plat_hold_band, ui_dialog_reach). GBA only; native tests switch it on
(talk_scene_hold). test_talk_hold.c: the same Talk run kept and full over a still backdrop is
the same picture on every frame at 240x160 and 320x240. The talk_dm steps run one a tick on
the GBA (talk_scene_slice was DC only).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Xd63cvyt9PpfrF57wBDFeR
